@page "/{*path}"

@* Every address no page claims. A route of its own, not the Router's NotFound: the Router answers
   a followed link to an address it does not know by reloading the page from the server, and a
   link with an anchor (release-notes#unreleased) cannot reload, since the browser only moves to
   the anchor. The Router then tries again, and the tab hangs in that loop. Here the address is
   matched, and the reader is told plainly that there is no page. *@
<PageTitle>Not found — ExGrid</PageTitle>

<MudText Typo="Typo.h4" HtmlTag="h1" Class="mt-8">Not found</MudText>
<MudText Class="mt-2">There is no page at this address. <MudLink Href="">Go to the start.</MudLink></MudText>

@code {
    /// <summary>The address no page claims.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Path { get; set; }
}
